      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hey @{6765b44b612cee9b76cb5d92|full_name} thanks for reporting this! Just want to clarify that there's indeed a mismatch between our documentation and the class definition. `OnPersistenceUsageUpdated` should output `void` (this is the bug to fix in our docs), however it should not take any params. Hope that helps, we'll keep this report open to update once the documentation fix is deployed",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-11-27T09:53:24.196Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In UdonSharpBehaviour class, the available method for OnPersistenceUsageUpdated is:\n\npublic virtual void OnPersistenceUsageUpdated()\n\nIt has no parameters, so the following documented signature cannot be overridden:\n\npublic virtual void OnPersistenceUsageUpdated(VRCPlayerApi player)\n\nTrying to override the documented version results in a compiler error.\n\nIt would be helpful to clarify whether the no-argument version is intentional (i.e., always referring to the local player), or if the UdonSharp stub is missing the correct signature.",
